;; THE LIMIT VALUES OF KOTOBA. One file; every other number is a copy of one
;; of these, and a copy is checked against this file.
;;
;; Authority: superproject adr-2609242100-kotoba-safety-is-language-resource-
;; is-target-profile, section 3 ("上限値の正本"). Step P1 of that ADR made this
;; file (2026-09-24). What the ADR decides, in one line each:
;;
;;   * what a program may DO is language; how much it may USE and how it is
;;     STOPPED is the target profile;
;;   * the static shape of a program (type descriptors, literal sizes, source
;;     size) is checked ONCE, at compile time  -> :language/static;
;;   * a value that arrives from outside is validated ONCE, at its boundary,
;;     against a traversal budget              -> :language/boundary;
;;   * resource budgets (fuel, cells, bytes, frames) are per-target defaults a
;;     caller may override per run             -> :profile/<target>.
;;
;; :language/value is the fourth section, and it is TRANSITIONAL. It records
;; the structural bounds every runtime still re-checks on internal values
;; today. The ADR removes them from internal values (P2 for the reference
;; interpreter, P3 for ESM / cljs / Wasm hosts); until then they are real,
;; they are enforced, and a runtime that disagrees with another about them
;; compiles a program one target runs and another traps on -- which is the
;; drift P1 fixes. When P2/P3 land, an entry here moves to :language/boundary
;; or is deleted, in the same commit as the code.
;;
;; SHAPE OF AN ENTRY
;;
;;   {:value   <integer>
;;    :why     "<one line>"
;;    :copies  [{:repo "kotoba-lang/<repo>" :path "<file>" :name "<constant>"} ...]}
;;
;; `:copies` names every place that restates the number, so the next person
;; to change it knows what moves with it. A copy with `:var` is compared by
;; resolving that var; one with `:pattern` is compared by reading the file's
;; source text (JS, C, and emitted preludes have no var). The comparison lives
;; in amu `test/kotoba/compiler/value_bounds_agreement_test.cljk` (amu is the
;; one repository with every runtime on its classpath) and, for the copies in
;; this repository, `test/kotoba/lang/limits_test.cljk`.
;;
;; Changing a value: change it here, run both tests, move every copy they name
;; in the same wave. A value changed here alone turns both tests red, by name.

{:kotoba.lang.limits/version 1
 :kotoba.lang.limits/adr "adr-2609242100-kotoba-safety-is-language-resource-is-target-profile"

